# Tool directories — cloned fresh by install.sh
BindCraft/
# BindCraft 2 is pre-publication and source-available under its own (non-MIT)
# licence. No file of it belongs in this MIT repo -- not even its LICENSE or
# README. It is unpacked here by the installer from --bc2-source, so the tree
# is present on disk on any machine that has it; without this line a plain
# `git add -A` on this branch stages 157 of its source files.
BindCraft2/
BoltzGen/
Mosaic/
PXDesign/
Proteina-Complexa/
Protein-Hunter/
LigandMPNN/
rf_diffusion_all_atom/

# Local Miniforge3 installation (standalone mode)
conda/

# Local shortcuts (standalone mode)
bin/

# Per-tool install-success markers written by install.sh and read by the
# configurator. Machine-local state, one file per tool, never shared.
.install_state/
.install_state.migrated

# Installer logs — ephemeral, can be large.
# NOT `install*.log`: that glob has no slash, so git matches it against the
# basename, and `install*` requires the name to START with "install".
# af3_install.log carries it in the middle and escaped for months.
*install*.log

# Claude Code internal files (settings, history, etc.) — but DO track .claude/skills/
.claude/*
!.claude/skills/

# Machine-local Claude Code notes (per-workstation setup, IPs, key paths) — never shared
CLAUDE.local.md
docs/local/

# Docker build cache / test artifacts
.docker-iidfile

# Run outputs — generated per-experiment
runs/
refold_boltz2/
# Shared target-MSA cache written by the refold engines at runtime
# (ColabFold hits, keyed by target-sequence hash).
msa_cache/
# Refold resume checkpoints and scratch outputs, written to the CWD by the
# refold engines. These four are all {"interrupted": true} -- the residue of
# runs killed by the GB10 guard and the 2026-09-21 freeze.
checkpoint_refold_*.json
refold_designs.csv
refold_designs.txt

# RFD3 / foundry checkpoints — fetched by `foundry install` (~2.5 GB), not part of repo
weights/

# AlphaFold 3 model weights — personal, DO NOT commit
af3.bin
*.af3.bin*

# RFD3 / ProteinMPNN foundry checkpoints (fetched by 'foundry install'; 2.5GB+)
weights/foundry/

# Evaluator build / runtime artefacts
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
Evaluator/envs/mosaic_venv_path
.venv/
# AlphaFold 3 clone dir — installed locally on Spark, not part of repo
alphafold3/

# Investigation analysis artifacts (regenerated by notebooks/_analysis.py)
notebooks/_artifacts/

# SoluProt USEARCH: the installer source-builds usearch12 (GPLv3) into this
# directory, so none of it is tracked — an MIT repo must not redistribute the
# binaries (they were removed in 2ae1bdb) and a bare arch-ambiguous 'usearch'
# once clobbered the x86 build across a branch merge.
Evaluator/tools/soluprot/usearch
Evaluator/tools/soluprot/usearch.x86_64
Evaluator/tools/soluprot/usearch.aarch64
Evaluator/tools/soluprot/usearch12-src/

# superpowers SDD scratch workspace
.superpowers/

# ── User campaign data: never commit research output to this public repo ──
# The documented workflow (see the orchestrator/worker skills) produces result
# packages, a cross-machine PROGRESS.md and per-machine assignment docs. None of
# those belong in git: a public repo is not a data store, and designed binder
# sequences are unpublished IP. Added 2026-10-27 after an audit found real
# campaign data committed under docs/data/.
# Prepared target structures: outputs of `prepare_target_pdb` (tag-trimmed,
# ligand-stripped) plus their extracted sequences. Derived working files for a
# campaign, regenerated by the configurator from the deposited structure, so they
# are inputs-in-progress rather than source. *.pdb already covers the structures;
# this adds the sequence sidecars and keeps the directory itself out.
targets_clean/
*.seq

RESULTS/
CLUSTER/
PROGRESS.md

# Scheduler and run logs (only *install*.log was covered before)
slurm-*.out
slurm-*.err
*.err

# Structure, sequence and array data. Design outputs and target structures are
# the two things most likely to be committed by accident — a user drops a .pdb
# at the repo root, or an evaluate/ report dir lands outside runs/.
*.pdb
*.cif
*.cif.gz
*.a3m
*.npz
*.fasta
*.fa

# …but the bundled upstream SoluProt training data IS tracked, and test or
# example fixtures must stay committable. Negate only the data extensions above
# — a blanket "!tests/**" would also un-ignore __pycache__/ (ignored at the top
# of this file), and a plain `pytest` run would then be staged by `git add -A`.
!Evaluator/tools/soluprot/data/**
!tests/**/*.pdb
!tests/**/*.cif
!tests/**/*.a3m
!tests/**/*.npz
!tests/**/*.fasta
!tests/**/*.fa
!bindmaster_examples/**/*.pdb
!bindmaster_examples/**/*.cif
!bindmaster_examples/**/*.fasta
!bindmaster_examples/**/*.fa

# docs/data/ was where the audited leak actually lived (benchmark CSVs carrying
# designed binder + target sequences). Ignore it wholesale; un-ignore a specific
# file deliberately if genuinely-public reference data ever belongs in the docs.
docs/data/

# TmProt is cloned at install time, never vendored: upstream is GPL-3.0 (its
# tmprot-1.0/setup.py says LGPLv3) and this repository is MIT.
Evaluator/tools/tmprot/
